<h2 style="text-align: center;">Prayer Of Redemption</h2>
<p>“Yehovah in the Name of Yeshua, according to the terms of your new covenant described in Jeremiah 31:31-34, you offer a covenant similar to the covenant made to the children of Israel in Exodus 19:5-6 when they were offered a covenant to ‘hear and obey’ and become a peculiar treasure and a reign of priests and a set-apart nation unto Yehovah. In that covenant, the children of Israel refused to hear and obey and requested Moses to intercede between You and the children of Israel instead. Thus, they broke Your covenant. However, in Your new covenant, the Torah is written upon our hearts and inward parts, and we are filled with the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit) who will lead us in all truth and will remind us of all Yeshua said and did.</p>

<p>Therefore, I have reviewed the terms of Your covenant to ‘hear and obey’ and agree to the terms of Your covenant today. I confess that Yeshua, the only begotten Son of Yehovah, laid down His life for me and ratified the New Covenant with His own blood and became the Lamb of Yehovah and took my punishment upon His body.</p>

<p>I ask that You forgive me of my sins, known and unknown, and ask You to wash me clean with the Blood of Yeshua. I ask that You help me become clean and forgive, and You will also forgive me.</p>
<p>Yehovah, today I receive the Ruach HaKodesh (the Holy Spirit) who will teach me and remind me of all Yeshua said in His Word. I know the Ruach HaKodesh will abide in me and will testify of Yeshua, the Lamb of Yehovah.</p>

<p>Thank you, Yehovah for my redemption and my life in You. I belong to Yeshua, and Yeshua belongs to Elohim. Amen.”</p>
